message.content:
You are the examiner of the live-spec intake chain (экзамен связного). Purpose: determine with evidence whether the designed chain works when actually driven, and where exactly it breaks. This is an EVIDENCE run — nothing you produce merges anywhere.

Read first: /private/tmp/live-spec-control/chain-canon-2026-08-18.md (the owner's verbatim canon + as-built state + known break points) and the exam protocol section of /private/tmp/live-spec-control/PLAN-2026-08-17.md.

Setup: cd /Users/sashaabramovich/live-spec && git worktree add /private/tmp/live-spec-exam/wt -b exam/2026-08-18 origin/main && cd /private/tmp/live-spec-exam/wt. All writes ONLY inside this worktree and the final report file. Never touch other worktrees, ~/.claude, protected files (.live-spec/PROBLEMS.md, culling-plan, docs/PROGRESS.md). No reset/rebase/stash/clean.

Pick 3 REAL unprocessed owner requests: look in inbox/ and FEEDBACK.md of the worktree (genuine owner wishes, ideally one likely-local, one likely-cross-cutting, one ambiguous). Quote each verbatim in the report.

For each request, drive the DESIGNED chain exactly as the method prescribes (use the pack's own skills as written — spec-author's completeness pass / delta assembly / merge-of-duplicates, the classification step (footprint/delta) even though it is not armed, traceability links):
1. triage: новое требование / правка существующего / вопрос / отказ + сквозной/локальный + раздел/подфункционал — with the written reason;
2. weave into PRODUCT_SPEC at the right place (worktree edit): merge with duplicates, update neighbours — record whether the method made this findable or you had to brute-search 703KB;
3. feature link into ARCHITECTURE: which node, update it;
4. TEST_MATRIX rows added, linked to the feature;
5. scoped test selection: name which tests the matrix rows imply, run THAT subset (not the full suite);
6. run the register/traceability checks that the method requires for a spec change.

Judge each request against the 7 criteria in the plan (1, 2, 2б, 3, 3б, 4 — spawn a fresh cold-reader subagent (sonnet) as the non-technical reader for the touched spec section, 5 — for prover, run the prover pack's prescribed review mode on the touched section if runnable locally; if the prover needs the external canon that is not installed, record that honestly as «прувер недоступен на машине: довыпиловочная копия» — that itself is an exam finding).

Deliverable: /private/tmp/live-spec-control/exam-report-2026-08-18.md, plain Russian, ≤80 lines: per request — verdict per criterion (сдал/провалил + one-line evidence), where the chain broke and WHY (cost of finding the place? classifier not armed? missing link?), and the closing section: (a) общий вердикт «связной сдал/провалил прогон 1»; (b) would arming the existing classifier have prevented each failure (да/нет + why); (c) would a semantic retrieval index have changed the cost materially (да/нет + measured evidence: how long/how many reads it took you to find the right place); (d) the exact repair list for tomorrow's second run. Return the same summary to me (≤25 lines). Leave the worktree in place with your spec edits uncommitted or committed locally (your choice), clearly stated.

